          <Properties>
            <Configuration>
              <Text>The tools in this container exist to adjust [Vintage Expected Losses] based on credit quality (Credit Score). 

Generally, a CECL reserve supported by the Vintage Methodology will have at least 3 years of charge off history to be effective. To limit the likelihood that sample size or data availability issues impact the [Vintage Adjustment], we will only unitize

Loans originated over the past 5 years, calculated as if DateTimeYear([Report Date])-DateTimeYear([Origination Date]) &lt; 6 then 1 else 0 endif

Loans charged off over the past 36 months, calculated as if DateTimeDiff([Report Date],[Charge Off Date],'months')&lt;36 then 1 else 0 endif

We define segment as [FICO TIER]+[[ALLOWANCE GROUP]+[VINTAGE YEAR].  To address anomalies and sample size issues we eliminate segments with either less than 200,000 in original balances or greater than a 25% charge off rate. An average of charge off rates by [FICO TIER]+[ALLOWANCE GROUP] is applied as the credit risk level charge off rate. 

With this same data, we will then calculate average 'base charge off rates' at the level of [ALLOWANCE GROUP]+[VINTAGE YEAR]. These rates, ignoring risk, will be compared to the rates seen at the [ALLOWANCE GROUP]+[FICO TIER] level to determine a [Vintage Adjustment]

We have put in place a control to ensure that a riskier [FICO TIER] may not have a favorable [Vintage Adjustment] as compared to a less risky [FICO TIER]. We've done this by sorting by [ALLOWANCE GROUP] and [FICO TIER] and incorporating a multi-row formula 

if [Row-1:Allowance Group]=[Allowance Group] and [Row-1:Avg_Charge Off % by FICO_Vintage_Group]&gt;[Avg_Charge Off % by FICO_Vintage_Group] then [Row-1:Avg_Charge Off % by FICO_Vintage_Group] else [Avg_Charge Off % by FICO_Vintage_Group] endif

[Vintage Adjustment] is then joined back into the loan data using [FICO TIER] and [ALLOWANCE GROUP]. [Vintage Adjusted Expected Losses] is calculated as [Vintage Expected Losses]*[Vintage Adjustment]</Text>
